## Vendored or linked into this repository

| Project | URL | License | What we take | Where |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| QEMU | https://www.qemu.org | GPL-2.0 | the fork under `qemu/` (submodule) | `qemu/` |
| Apple XNU | https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/xnu | APSL-2.0 | patches applied to the kernel we build | `xnu/*.patch` |
| HakiOS APFS tools | https://github.com/oosexgang/hakios-xnu-kernel | MIT | `apfs.py` and `mkapfs.py`, verbatim except for an SPDX/provenance header: the APFS container writer that lets a Linux host build the guest's system image | `tools/apfs/` |

`tools/apfs/mkapfs.py` is the one piece of third-party code this project depends on at run time for
M1: it writes the APFS container that `tools/make-images.sh` produces. It was chosen over writing our
own because it is validated upstream by `apfsck` and by the kernel reading every volume back, and
because a filesystem writer with no test suite of its own is how images get silently corrupt. Its
output is checked here the same way (`apfsck`, plus a 7-Zip read-back through a different parser).
The vendored copies were taken at upstream commit `a3384e0`; see the header of each file.

`LICENSE.GPL2` carries the QEMU text; `LICENSE.APSL` carries the APSL-2.0 text.

